  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this problem: Command Palette stopping \\\"|\\\" from being typed in non-elevated apps while it works in elevated ones. The closest tickets are different problems. PowerToys#47617 is a French AZERTY ticket where AltGr+- triggers Text Extractor instead of typing \\\"|\\\". PowerToys#46790 is about dropped letters in the Currency Converter, which was fixed by an update. Please keep this ticket open as a new bug. Add your keyboard layout and the exact key combination you use for \\\"|\\\". Also say whether Command Palette's \\\"Use low-level keyboard hook\\\" setting is on, and attach a PowerToys bug report ZIP. In the meantime, you can turn Command Palette off to type \\\"|\\\" normally. You can also try turning off the low-level keyboard hook in Command Palette settings, but I can't confirm that helps.\"}",
